<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicolas Perrenot de Granvelle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1486–1550</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nicolas Perrenot de Granvelle was a lawyer from Franche-Comté who rose to become one of the chief ministers of the Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, serving as his keeper of the seals and principal adviser on imperial affairs from the 1530s. He built the Palais Granvelle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besancon">Besançon</a>, now a museum. His son Antoine Perrenot de Granvelle became a cardinal and a leading minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicolas-perrenot-de-granvelle.jpg" alt="Nicolas Perrenot de Granvelle" width="320" height="381" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Attributed to Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tizian-Nicolas_Granvelle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
